✅ Q13 — Find the First Number That Appears Only Once

🎗️ 13.1 Problem Statement

You are given a List<Integer> containing positive, negative, and zero values.
Using Java Streams, find the first number that appears exactly once in the list.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Return the result as an Integer.
🔴 Preserve the original encounter order.
🔴 Correctly handle positive and negative integers.
🔴 Correctly handle duplicate values.
🔴 Correctly handle zero.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty list.
🔴 Return an appropriate result when no unique number exists.

🎗️ 13.2 Input / Output

👉 Input List :
List<Integer> numbers = List.of(10, 25, 10, -5, 40, 25, 15, -5, 30, 25);

👉 Expected Output : 40

Because:

10 → appears 2 times ❌
25 → appears 3 times ❌
-5 → appears 2 times ❌
40 → appears 1 time ✅
15 → appears 1 time ✅
30 → appears 1 time ✅

The first number that appears exactly once is: 40

🎗️ 13.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.
You can provide:

🔴 Your primary approach
🔴 Any alternative approaches — Streams only
🔴 Your thoughts about empty-list behavior
🔴 How you preserve encounter order
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt those too.